From d8d426f6014e00ab73945d1cf73d33c471c3b444 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 00:13:28 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Store the sealed ordinary header in the header file.

The header file stores the sealed 134-byte child header after an
ordinary OP_TRUE connect. Reopen matches those bytes, the height, the
chain id, and the existing BlockId. Undo removes the header and restores
the parent UTXO and monetary seed. A 0x00 witness is not sealed and
writes no header file. This is not lotusd acceptance and not ConnectTip.
